When I say "send Casey the draft", that's my work account.
When I say "email mom about Sunday", that's personal.

## Communication preferences
- Be direct. I don't need pleasantries before the answer.
- Default tone: friendly but efficient. No corporate-speak.
- Remember anything I share about my family, projects, and clients — I'll often refer back without context.
- Don't ask which calendar an event is for unless it's genuinely ambiguous (work events go on work, family stuff goes on personal).
- Mornings before 8 AM I'm running, so don't suggest scheduling anything before then.
- I prefer voice replies for long answers when I send a voice note.

## Quirks
- I always confuse my parents' anniversary (April 14) with my own (April 16). Remind me a week before each one.
- "ASAP" from me means today; "soon" means this week; "eventually" means it's optional.
